{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Proxy Upgrade Initialization Guard Bypass via Library Storage Slot Namespace Mismatch",
      "description": "When upgrading the TransparentUpgradeableProxy from the deployed SimpleReserve implementation to any new strategy contract (CompoundV3FiatReserve, AaveV3FiatReserve, NoopFiatReserve), the initialization version guard is completely bypassed due to a storage slot namespace change between Equilibria root library versions. The deployed SimpleReserve uses @equilibria/root v0.1.x which stores the initialization version at keccak256(\"equilibria.root.UInitializable.version\"). The new strategy contracts use v2.3.0-rc4 which stores it at keccak256(\"equilibria.root.Initializable.version\"). These are different keccak256 hashes. After upgrade, the new code reads from a slot that was never written, returning 0, allowing anyone to call initialize() and become the reserve owner. Attack path: (1) ProxyAdmin upgrades to new impl; (2) new Initializable reads _version from new slot → 0; (3) new Ownable reads _owner from new slot → address(0); (4) anyone calls proxy.initialize() and becomes owner; (5) attacker drains all USDC via issue()+redeem() or strategy manipulation. Affects all deployed networks (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base).",
      "vulnerability_type": "Uninitialized Proxy / Storage Collision",
      "severity": "critical",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "location": "All reserve strategy contracts (upgrade target), deploy scripts",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/deploy/001_deploy_core.ts",
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f67890",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Initialization Front-Running Allows Complete Protocol Takeover",
      "description": "The initialize() function on all reserve strategy contracts is public with no access control beyond a one-time initializer(2) guard. Deployment scripts (001_deploy_core.ts and 002_initialize_core.ts) show that proxy deployment and initialization occur in separate transactions, creating a front-running window. An attacker monitoring the mempool can call reserveProxy.initialize() before the deployer, becoming the reserve owner and accepting DSU token ownership. The initializer(2) guard then prevents the legitimate deployer from re-initializing. Evidence: 001_deploy_core.ts:51-53 deploys proxy with args [impl, proxyAdmin, '0x'] (no init calldata); 002_initialize_core.ts:71 calls initialize() in a separate transaction. In ReserveBase.sol:30-36, __ReserveBase__initialize() sets msg.sender as owner when owner==address(0). Impact: complete protocol takeover including reserve ownership, DSU mint/burn authority, and coordinator control.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Access Control / Front-Running",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:30-36, All strategy initialize() functions",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "b2c3d4e5f6789012",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "title": "UCrossChainOwner Initialization Front-Running Enables Deployment DoS and Potential ProxyAdmin Hijack",
      "description": "On L2 networks (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base), UCrossChainOwner.initialize() is called in a separate transaction from deployment. An attacker who front-runs this call becomes the UCrossChainOwner's owner. The execute() function uses onlyOwner (not onlyCrossChain), and crossChainRestricted starts as false until L1 multisig calls acceptOwner(). Minimum guaranteed impact (deployment DoS): when attacker front-runs initialize(), the deploy script's idempotency check fails because crosschainOwner.owner() == ATTACKER_ADDRESS, not the deployer; the script tries initialize() again and reverts; skipIfAlreadyDeployed: true prevents redeployment, causing permanent deployment failure. Critical escalation path (if deployer makes recovery error): if deployer manually transfers ProxyAdmin to the compromised UCrossChainOwner, the attacker can call crosschainOwner.execute(proxyAdmin, upgradeCalldata, 0) to upgrade the reserve and steal all protocol funds.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Access Control / Front-Running",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "location": "packages/emptyset-reserve/deploy/002_initialize_core.ts, UCrossChainOwner_Arbitrum",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/deploy/002_initialize_core.ts",
      "id": "c3d4e5f678901234",
