    },
    {
      "title": "Missing Reentrancy Guards on mint() and redeem()",
      "description": "mint() and redeem() make 3-4 sequential external calls without a nonReentrant modifier: _pull() → fiat token transferFrom; _allocate() → strategy supply/withdraw (Compound/Aave); _mint()/_redeem() → DSU mint/burn; dsu.push()/dsu.pull() → DSU transfer. Currently NOT exploitable because USDC, Compound V3, Aave V3, and DSU are all plain ERC20s with no transfer callbacks. Risk: USDC is an upgradeable proxy. If Circle ever adds ERC-777-style callback support, all reserves become immediately vulnerable to reentrancy without any code change in the reserve contracts. Recommendation: add OpenZeppelin nonReentrant modifier to mint(), redeem(), and issue() as defense-in-depth.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:70-83",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "d4e5f67890123456",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zero-Amount Aave V3 Calls Cause DoS Due to 18-to-6 Decimal Precision Truncation",
      "description": "_update() in AaveV3FiatReserve converts 18-decimal UFixed18 amounts to 6-decimal UFixed6 via truncation. When collateral - target < 1e12 (sub-micro-USDC difference), UFixed6Lib.from() returns 0. Aave V3 reverts on 0-amount operations (require(amount != 0, Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT)), creating a temporary DoS on all mint/redeem until the coordinator changes allocation percentage or Aave interest accrual pushes collateral above target+1e12. Triggered naturally when allocation is a non-round fraction (e.g., 33%, 67%) and Aave interest creates sub-micro-USDC accounting drift. Does NOT affect CompoundV3FiatReserve — Compound V3 handles 0-amount operations as silent no-ops. Fix: guard against zero amounts before calling Aave: UFixed6 amount = UFixed6Lib.from(collateral.sub(target)); if (collateral.gt(target) && !amount.isZero()) aave.withdraw(fiat, amount, address(this));",
      "vulnerability_type": "Arithmetic / Denial of Service",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "location": "AaveV3FiatReserve.sol:65-69",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/AaveV3FiatReserve.sol",
      "id": "e5f6789012345678",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "title": "CompoundV3FiatReserve Targets USDC.e (Bridged USDC) Not Native USDC on Arbitrum",
      "description": "Integration tests confirm CompoundV3FiatReserve is configured for Compound's USDC.e market (0xA5EDBDD9646f8dFF606d7448e414884C7d905dCA on Arbitrum). Native USDC market is only used to test the error case. Since the constructor validates compound.baseToken() == fiat, the fiat token must be USDC.e. USDC.e is 'Bridged USDC' — NOT Circle's natively-issued USDC on Arbitrum. Circle launched native Arbitrum USDC in June 2023 and is encouraging migration. Risks: USDC.e/USDC peg risk if Arbitrum bridge is exploited; long-term deprecation risk as liquidity migrates to native USDC; Compound V3 USDC.e market deprecation risk. The fiat and compound constructor args are immutable — migration requires a proxy upgrade.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Configuration / Systemic Risk",
      "severity": "medium",
