    {
      "title": "ProxyAdmin Has Unconstrained Upgrade Power With No Timelock and Shared Owner",
      "description": "The reserve is behind a TransparentUpgradeableProxy with a ProxyAdmin. The ProxyAdmin owner can atomically deploy a malicious implementation and call upgrade() in a single transaction, giving users zero time to react. Additionally, the ProxyAdmin owner and Reserve owner are the SAME multisig address, violating separation of concerns. A single key compromise provides both operational control (issue, coordinator) AND unrestricted upgrade power. An upgrade to a malicious implementation could drain all reserve assets immediately. Recommendation: (1) add a timelock (48h+) on proxy upgrades; (2) use separate owners for ProxyAdmin and Reserve; (3) consider a governance module with upgrade delay.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Access Control / Governance",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.72,
      "location": "deploy/002_initialize_core.ts:59-65, proxy architecture",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/deploy/002_initialize_core.ts",
      "id": "1890123456789012",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Strategy Liquidity Failure Blocks All Reserve Mint and Redeem Operations",
      "description": "When allocation is high (e.g., 95%) and the strategy protocol has high utilization (normal DeFi condition), _allocate() during redeem() tries to withdraw more than the strategy has available, causing a revert. If Compound V3 or Aave V3 is paused or reverts on supply()/withdraw(), the _update() call in _allocate() reverts, blocking ALL mints and redeems with no fallback or try/catch. All users are locked out until strategy liquidity returns or the coordinator lowers allocation. This is a liveness failure under normal high-utilization conditions. Recommendation: wrap strategy calls in try/catch, add a circuit breaker, or implement partial-fill withdrawal logic.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Denial of Service / External Dependency",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.78,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:78-83, 127-131; CompoundV3FiatReserve.sol:60-65",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "2901234567890123",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Owner Can Front-Run Strategy Losses via issue() to Amplify Holder Losses",
      "description": "The owner can call issue() to extract the overcollateral buffer just before a known strategy loss event (e.g., Compound governance attack). Without the overcollateral buffer, per-holder losses are amplified. Example: with 10% overcollateral buffer, a 5% strategy loss reduces redeemPrice from 1.0 to 0.95. But if owner first extracts the 10% buffer via issue(), the same 5% loss reduces redeemPrice to approximately 0.86, nearly doubling the per-holder loss. The owner has informational advantage and can observe mempool transactions signaling an impending loss. Recommendation: add a minimum overcollateralization ratio and add a timelock to issue().",
      "vulnerability_type": "Economic / Trust Assumption",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": 0.68,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:86-91",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "3012345678901234",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Case Comparison Bug in Deploy Script Breaks Idempotency",
      "description": "The deploy script contains a case-sensitive string comparison that fails to correctly detect already-deployed contract state when the network name or address casing differs from what is stored. This breaks the idempotency guarantee of skipIfAlreadyDeployed: true, potentially causing the script to attempt re-deployment of already-deployed contracts or skip initialization of contracts that were deployed but not initialized. Confirmed as a low-severity but real defect in the deployment tooling.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Logic Error / Deployment",
      "severity": "low",
