      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "title": "No Slippage Protection on redeem() Allows Sandwich or Unfavorable Execution",
      "description": "redeem() has no minimum output amount parameter. The redeemPrice could change between transaction submission and execution if the owner calls issue() or a strategy suffers a loss. Users have no way to specify a minimum acceptable redemption amount, exposing them to unfavorable execution if redeemPrice decreases between submission and execution. Downgraded from Medium to Low because mintPrice=1 always (providing no practical slippage risk on minting) and redeemPrice changes slowly for a stablecoin reserve. Recommendation: add optional minAmount parameter: function redeem(UFixed18 amount, UFixed18 minRedemption).",
      "vulnerability_type": "Slippage Protection",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:78-83",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "5234567890123456",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Latent Bug in _mint() Uses Raw Amount Instead of Computed mintAmount",
      "description": "_mint() computes mintAmount = amount.mul(mintPrice()) but then calls IDSU(Token18.unwrap(dsu)).mint(UFixed18.unwrap(amount)), minting the raw amount rather than the computed mintAmount. These are only equal because mintPrice() always returns ONE. If mintPrice() is ever made dynamic (e.g., to implement a minting fee or spread), the minted amount would not match the amount returned by _mint(), silently breaking the accounting invariant that callers rely on. Fix: change the mint call to use UFixed18.unwrap(mintAmount).",
      "vulnerability_type": "Logic Error / Arithmetic",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": 0.82,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:97-102",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "6345678901234567",
