    },
    {
      "title": "renounceOwnership() Not Overridden on DSU — Can Permanently Brick Protocol",
      "description": "The DSU contract inherits renounceOwnership() from OZ Ownable via Ownable2Step. If the reserve contract (as DSU owner) ever calls renounceOwnership(), DSU ownership is permanently set to address(0). All DSU mint and burn operations require onlyOwner, so the DSU token becomes permanently unmintable and unburnable, effectively bricking the reserve system. New DSU cannot be issued and existing DSU cannot be redeemed. Recommendation: override renounceOwnership() to revert, or explicitly document this as an intentional emergency shutdown mechanism.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Access Control / Operational Risk",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "location": "DSU.sol (inherited from Ownable2Step → Ownable)",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/token/DSU.sol",
      "id": "7456789012345678",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Coordinator Can Force Instant Full Rebalance Causing Strategy Overflow DoS",
      "description": "The coordinator can change allocation from 0% to 100% (or any large delta) in a single transaction with no rate limiting. The next mint() or redeem() call triggers a massive rebalance that could hit strategy supply caps or fail due to liquidity limits in Compound V3 or Aave V3, causing a DoS on the reserve. There is no maximum per-period allocation change limit or ramp-up period. Recommendation: add rate limiting on allocation changes or a maximum delta per time window.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Denial of Service / Input Validation",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": 0.65,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:45-50",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "8567890123456789",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Read-Only Reentrancy on redeemPrice() During Composable Operations",
      "description": "During mint() or redeem() execution, between sequential external calls, contract state can be temporarily inconsistent (assets transferred but DSU not yet minted, or vice versa). External contracts reading redeemPrice() via callbacks during this window would see incorrect values. This is a concern for DeFi protocols that use redeemPrice() as an on-chain oracle for DSU valuation, as they could make pricing decisions based on a mid-execution price that does not reflect the true reserve state. Recommendation: document that redeemPrice() should not be used as a real-time oracle during composable operations; consider adding a reentrancy lock that prevents external reads of redeemPrice() during execution.",
      "vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy / Oracle Manipulation",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": 0.58,
      "location": "ReserveBase.sol:64-67",
      "file": "packages/emptyset-reserve/contracts/reserve/ReserveBase.sol",
      "id": "9678901234567890",
      "reported_by_model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "status": "proposed"
    },
    {
      "title": "Strategy Pause Blocks All Reserve Operations With No Emergency Escape",
      "description": "If Compound V3 or Aave V3 is paused or permanently reverts on supply()/withdraw(), the _update() call within _allocate() reverts, blocking ALL mints and redeems for all users. There is no try/catch, circuit breaker, or emergency bypass mechanism. The coordinator can lower allocation to 0% to restore functionality, but this requires an active coordinator response. If the coordinator is unavailable or the pause is permanent, all reserve operations are indefinitely blocked. Upgraded from Low to Medium because strategy pause creates a complete DoS for all users with no autonomous escape mechanism.",
